# Dry-run safety

By default, `CHILI_PRODUCTION_MODE=false`. External side effects are blocked and logged:

- Telegram messages (`notify_user`, `send`)
- Notion writes (`complete`, `publish_progress`, training sync)
- Device control (BroadLink, SwitchBot, display power)
- LLM API calls (OpenAI)

**Never set `CHILI_PRODUCTION_MODE=true` without explicit owner approval in the chat.**

The Pi's production `.env` enables it. CI, agent environments, and fresh checkouts are always in dry-run mode.
